{"text": "Mr Deputy Speaker,\n\nToday, | report on a Britain that is growing, creating jobs and paying its way.\n\nWe took difficult decisions in the teeth of opposition and it worked - Britain is\nwalking tall again.\n\nFive years ago, our economy had suffered a collapse greater than almost any\ncountry.\n\nToday, | can confirm: in the last year we have grown faster than any other\nmajor advanced economy in the world.\n\nFive years ago, millions of people could not find work.\n\nToday, | can report: more people have jobs in Britain than ever before.\n\nFive years ago, living standards were set back years by the Great Recession.\n\nToday, the latest projections show that living standards will be higher than\nwhen we came to office.\n\nFive years ago, the deficit was out of control.\n\nToday, as a Share of national income it is down by more than a half.\n\nFive years ago, we were bailing out the banks.",
